<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Chaonia</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Chaonia was the north-western region of ancient <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/epirus">Epirus</a>, on the Ionian coast in present-day southern Albania, home of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chaonians">Chaonians</a>, one of the three main Epirote peoples. Its chief town was <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/phoenice">Phoenice</a>, and Butrint lay within it. The Chaonians were at first governed by an aristocracy rather than kings, and later joined the Epirote state and the league that followed the monarchy.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/chaonia.jpg" alt="Chaonia" width="320" height="214" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Geoff Wong · CC BY 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Amphitheatre_of_Butrint_2009.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
